## Distinguish Knowledge Store listing failures during deletion

Context: A final concrete-store review found that Lakebase document-listing
failures degraded to an empty list, allowing version deletion to report
success after metadata removal without proving Knowledge Store cleanup.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py
   Added an opt-in strict document-listing contract while preserving tolerant defaults for existing read-only callers.
2. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py
   Made strict listing raise StoreError for unavailable document tables and query failures while preserving genuine empty results.
3. src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py
   Opted destructive version cleanup into strict listing after the atomic Draft-guarded metadata deletion.
